{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the SGD 6.00 CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) gantry line on EV-FARE-00532 is unmatched by the GPS trace (nearest fix 1159.02 m from the gantry, outside the 250 m crossing radius); it is refunded in full as a standalone correction and is flagged for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.90,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This is an upfront-quoted trip: EV-FARE-00532 shows fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 75.00 and total_charged 81.00. Everything below is read off those figures.\n\nDistance and time: the rider's claim fails at the first gate. The governing measurement is the trace, not the rounded copy. EV-GPS-00532 records trace_distance_km 31.49 against the 28.0 km optimal route on EV-TRIP-00532 — an excess of 3.49 km, or 12.46%. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH limbs to pass: the absolute limb (0.8 km) passes, but the percentage limb (over 20%) does not, and the derived deviation block itself returns 'no deviation'. No deviation is established, so no distance-or-time refund arises. Independently, POL-RD-11 fixes the distance and time charges at booking on an upfront-quoted trip, so the 75.00 of base, distance, time and platform fee stands untouched however large the excess. The rider's argument that the trip was longer than it should have been cannot move that money.\n\nERP: the one line that does move is the SGD 6.00 ERP charge on EV-FARE-00532 for the CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) gantry. Matching the gantry's stated coordinates (lat 1.37, lng 103.847) against the trace, the closest of the 289 fixes is 1159.02 m away — far outside the 250 m radius POL-RD-09 uses to treat a fix as a crossing, and the trace never brackets the gantry. The gantry is therefore unmatched, the line is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), and it is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not any deviation exists. Both sides effectively converge on this: the driver does not resist the 6.00, and the rider's remedy under POL-RD-11(a) — the amount by which 81.00 exceeds the 75.00 quote plus only properly chargeable pass-through lines — is the same 6.00, because the ERP line is not properly chargeable. So 81.00 less 75.00 = 6.00 is returned, and no more.\n\nThe rider's remaining points add no money. The suggestion that a second passenger was collected is unsupported by any artifact: vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary analysis is not engaged; the chat log EV-CHAT-00532 holds zero messages; no rider track exists; and in any event the entire measured excess (3.49 km) is already inside a sub-threshold figure. The rider's belief that the platform already refunded half is contradicted by the very ledger he relies on: EV-FARE-00532 shows refund_issued_sgd 0.00 and payment_status CHARGED.\n\nThe driver's explanation that local roads were faster does not need to be reached, because no deviation is established; and to the extent it is offered as a traffic excuse, the only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00532-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload), so under POL-RD-08 a general assertion that traffic was bad does not discharge anything.\n\nConfidence and escalation: the deciding fact — that the gantry was not crossed — is carried by EV-GPS-00532 and EV-FARE-00532, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The absent advisory carries no weight and does not cap this ruling. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired (289 fixes, 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, zero gaps), the trip identifiers all match, and the only charge line without a trace counterpart is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excepts. A POL-RD-06 conduct referral is not warranted either (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 250). The only referral is the billing-integrity one above."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity review: the SGD 6.00 ERP charge for the CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) gantry is unmatched to the GPS trace (nearest fix 1,159.02 m, outside the 250 m match radius) and is refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider, you are partly right: SGD 6.00 of the SGD 81.00 you were charged is refunded to you, and the remaining SGD 75.00 stands. Driver, you keep the SGD 75.00 fare; the only charge that moves is the ERP line.\n\nDistance and time (both advocates agree, and I accept it). The governing measurement is the trace: EV-GPS-00532 records 31.49 km against an optimal route of 28.00 km, an excess of 3.49 km, or 12.46%. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to exceed BOTH 20% of optimal distance and 0.8 km absolute; the percentage limb fails, so no deviation is established and the deriived deviation block correctly returns 'no deviation'. The rounded 31.5 km on the trip record cannot be cited for the threshold test, and even it yields only 12.5%. Independently, this is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip (quoted fare SGD 75.00 on EV-FARE-00532), so POL-RD-02 does not run and POL-RD-11 gives you no distance-or-time refund however large the excess. The rider's suggestion that a second passenger was collected changes nothing and is unsupported: vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, solo_optimal_distance_km is null, the chat log holds 0 messages and the trace carries no rider track; POL-RD-12 is not engaged.\n\nThe one charge that moves (SGD 6.00). You were charged charged_total SGD 81.00 = the SGD 75.00 quote + a SGD 6.00 ERP line for the CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) gantry. POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trip by treating any fix within 250 m as a crossing. The closest of the 289 fixes lies 1,159.02 m away, so the gantry is never passed and the line is one the rider did not incur. It is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4) and is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists: 81.00 - 75.00 = 6.00. The same figure follows from POL-RD-11(a), because the 6.00 is the only amount by which the charge exceeds the quote plus properly chargeable pass-throughs, and no pass-through is properly chargeable here. Driver, your own statement that 'local roads were faster' is consistent with the trace and confirms the gantry was not crossed; the ERP cannot be passed through for a gantry the vehicle never reached.\n\nOther points. The claim that the platform already refunded half is not borne out: EV-FARE-00532 records payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and POL-GEN-03 leaves that present state standing save for the 6.00 above. The missing advisory EV-ADVIS-00532-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) carried no fact this ruling needs, so it neither excuses the route nor drags confidence. No escalation trigger fires: the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07 (289 fixes at 10 s, 100% coverage, zero gaps, max gap 0.0 s), the trip identifiers all match, and the only charge line without a counterpart in the trace is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excepts. The driver's no-repeat-pattern point (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 250 trips) is accepted and moot; it is also the only reason no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral issues.\n\nConfidence is 0.90, capped by the deciding artifacts EV-GPS-00532 and EV-FARE-00532, each at weight_multiplier 1.0. All figures are read off EV-FARE-00532 and EV-GPS-00532. A POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral rides with this ruling."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
